diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 18032a4..1e433fe 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - **Failures name the selector on Android** — `Element not visible: text='X'`, `Element not found for swipe: text='X'` (iOS too; where an element swipe starts is now documented in docs/selectors.md), with the closest on-screen texts as the cause; a timed-out notVisible check says `Element still visible: text='X' after 10s` on both platforms.
 
 ### Fixed
+- **Android launch crash decisions recheck matching fatal logs immediately before success.** A fatal arriving after the first-frame snapshot now fails `launchApp`; crashes after return remain covered by the next step's watch.
+- **Android failure screenshots, hierarchy and app log tails run concurrently with cancellable deadlines.** Screenshot capture uses the server socket, successful artifacts survive another collector timing out, and report artifacts include per-collector notes. Cancellation waits for the request or owned shell child to finish.
 - **Android `launchApp` passed on an app that crashed right after its first frame** — once `Displayed` was logged, a crash recorded for the launched pid no longer counted, so `99-crash` passed `launchApp` 1-3 s after the crash and failed at the next step. A FATAL EXCEPTION or `am_crash` of a launched pid now fails the launch with `app_crash` whether or not the first frame was logged first, and a launch none of whose processes runs after the first frame was read fails as well. On the default software-rendered AVD `launchApp` failed within 2 s of the FATAL EXCEPTION (0.4-0.55 s in 10 runs, all caught by the launch). A crash that comes after the launch passed fails the next step through the post-launch watch, which checks every 250 ms; that path is covered by a unit test, as no device run produced it.
 - **Android `doubleTapOn` still counted as two taps on a software-rendered AVD** — the W3C pointer sequence is injected event by event, each stamped when injected and waiting for the app, so its 200 ms took 0.7-1.3 s and the app counted two single taps in 4 of 5 runs; the server's own `double_click` (1.1-1.35 s) never counted as one. The on-device double tap above is one double tap in 5 of 5 runs.
 - **`waitForAnimationToEnd` passed on an app that had crashed after launch** (iOS and Android). The home screen or launcher left on screen is static, so the settle passed in half a second and a screens flow captured it as the screen. While the app the last `launchApp` started is watched, the settle now fails with `app_crash` (`app crashed: <bundle> is not running` on iOS, the FATAL EXCEPTION on Android); after an intentional `stopApp`, `killApp` or `clearState` it passes as before.
